# CHARACTER VARIANT — SANDY: FOGGED GLASS VARIANT

Status: episode-specific character variant for S14-E20 "The Violet Distance".

Base character: Sandy / Sandy Hourglass [CH_01]

## Purpose

This is not a new story character. It is an episode-specific visual/behavioral variant of Sandy used for scenes where Perfume Madame’s violet mist affects him.

The variant exists because the locked base Sandy asset cannot be edited directly and does not contain enough textual description for the complex mist/allergy/emotional distortion behavior required in S14-E20.

## Core Identity

Sandy remains the same soft transparent hourglass hero with golden sand as his life resource.

He is:
- active,
- emotionally pulled forward,
- physically vulnerable,
- trying to get closer,
- trying to control his reaction,
- and failing in visible physical comedy.

## Episode-Specific Visual Behavior

When Sandy enters Perfume Madame’s violet mist, his transparent body reacts.

Effects:
- inner fogging on the glass/silicone surface;
- condensation-like patches inside the body;
- golden sand becomes less stable;
- sand may swirl, clog, pulse, or form uneven piles;
- the narrow waist may appear tense or temporarily blocked;
- rubber limbs stretch toward Perfume Madame, then recoil;
- eyes water, distort, or blink uncontrollably;
- body bends forward from attraction, then snaps backward from allergic reaction.

## Shape Language

Sandy keeps his recognizable hourglass silhouette.

Do not redesign him into a new character.

Allowed changes:
- fogged translucent body;
- slightly more nervous posture;
- mist wrapping around edges;
- subtle violet reflections on the transparent surface;
- sand temporarily displaced by emotional pressure;
- exaggerated squash and stretch under allergy bursts.

Not allowed:
- changing his base anatomy;
- replacing the golden sand;
- making him opaque;
- making him look like a different species;
- adding complex costume details;
- turning him into a realistic glass object.

## Material

Sandy’s body is transparent soft silicone / glass-like material.

In this variant it becomes:
- fogged,
- slightly wet-looking,
- internally clouded by violet mist,
- still readable with bold black outline.

The golden sand remains warm and alive. It should contrast against the cool violet haze.

## Comedy Function

The comedy comes from the contradiction:

**Sandy wants to move closer emotionally, but his own body treats closeness as a physical allergy.**

His body betrays him in visible ways:
- fogging,
- sneezing-like body spasms,
- sand turbulence,
- rubber-limb recoil,
- awkward attempts to look normal,
- sudden loss of balance.

## Interaction with Perfume Madame

Perfume Madame’s violet mist should never fully hide Sandy.

The mist should:
- wrap around him,
- enter the transparent body visually,
- create internal fogging,
- push him back,
- distort his perception,
- create romantic/emotional attraction and allergic rejection at the same time.

## First Visual Prompt

2D flat cartoon character design, Sandy Hourglass episode-specific fogged glass variant, soft transparent hourglass body with warm golden sand inside, bold black outlines, rubber glove-like dark grey arms, simple flexible legs, body partially fogged from inside by violet perfume mist, condensation-like cloudy patches on transparent surface, golden sand swirling unevenly and slightly clogged at the narrow waist, nervous romantic expression, watery eyes, body leaning forward while rubber arms recoil, subtle violet reflections, action-first readable silhouette, classic 2D comedic animation style, clean vector shapes, simple neutral background, no text --no photorealism, no 3d render, no realistic glass, no over-detailed smoke, no costume, no opaque body, no human proportions

## Negative Prompt / Restrictions

- do not redesign Sandy’s base silhouette;
- do not remove the hourglass body;
- do not replace golden sand;
- do not make him opaque;
- do not add clothing or complex accessories;
- do not make him realistic glass;
- do not hide the character inside smoke;
- do not use text or labels in the image.
```

